decision: changes-requested

Four medium blockers remain:

- **N1** — [review_dispatch.go:1027](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2552678434/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1027): if subreaper setup fails, cleanup silently skips the orphan scan.
- **N2** — [review_dispatch.go:1028](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2552678434/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1028): an unreadable start-time cutoff defaults to zero, which can select pre-existing processes.
- **N3** — [review_reap_linux.go:110](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2552678434/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:110): an unreadable process start time can be mistaken for a baseline process, allowing cleanup to succeed without accounting for it.
- **N4** — [review_reap_linux.go:68](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2552678434/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:68): a reviewer-controlled process name is persisted without credential redaction.

The three R6 findings are fixed; the focused regression tests and `go vet` passed. `surface-check` passed. Both strict validation commands could not create Go build/cache files in the read-only sandbox, so they are deferred against the supplied sealed evidence. The required completion checks were deferred; `review-check` also reported a local sealed-input freshness mismatch. The dispatched engine accepted the final draft, and the working tree is clean.

